{"parentUuid":"3dcc117c-3017-4b79-8ce9-15c1e13f99d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KmVJtSSKYuWc2gLVCFkDk3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bug reproduced and committed as a skipped regression test (`71b85ad39`).\n\n**Findings from the reproduction:**\n\nThe bug fires when **all** of these are true:\n1. The stale session is ACTIVE with `LastInteractionTime` within 24h.\n2. `sessionsWithCommittedFiles == 0` at gate-check time — meaning **no** session's on-disk `state.FilesTouched` overlaps with the committed file set.\n3. The stale session has a transcript file with *some* content (even just a startup banner).\n4. The stale session's `state.FilesTouched` is empty and the live transcript yields no file modifications via extraction.\n\nCondition 2 is the hidden one. In the real Codex/Claude scenario, the working Claude session must have had `state.FilesTouched` empty on disk at the moment `git post-commit` fired — likely because the tool-use hooks that merge file modifications into the on-disk state hadn't run between SaveStep and the commit, or `condenseAndUpdateState` cleared it after a previous condensation and the next SaveStep hadn't repopulated it yet. The shadow branch still had the actual content (so the working session condensed correctly), but the on-disk count went to 0, the read-only-skip in `shouldCondenseWithOverlapCheck` didn't fire, and the stale session slipped through.\n\nOnce past the gate, `extractSessionDataFromLiveTranscript` returns a non-empty `Transcript` with empty `FilesTouched`, `sessionHasEvidenceOfWork` flags it as a real participant on the transcript-non-empty branch, and `filterFilesTouched` assigns the committed files to it.\n\n**Two reasonable fixes** (still your call):\n1. **Tighten the gate** in `shouldCondenseWithOverlapCheck` so a stale session's lack of *any evidence of work this checkpoint window* (no recent transcript growth, no SaveStep contributions to the shadow branch) is enough to skip it, independent of `sessionsWithCommittedFiles`.\n2. **Tighten `sessionHasEvidenceOfWork`** so it requires per-window evidence (transcript growth past `CheckpointTranscriptStart`, or SaveStep contributions in this base-commit window) rather than just \"any transcript content / lifetime StepCount > 0\".\n\nI'd lean toward (1) — it's simpler and stops the inheritance at the gate before condensation runs at all. Want me to implement that fix on this branch, or split it off?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":111,"cache_read_input_tokens":372799,"output_tokens":835,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":111,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":835,"cache_read_input_tokens":372799,"cache_creation_input_tokens":111,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":111},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CajA5aqon48vc74fkgWy3","type":"assistant","uuid":"be7e4b79-e26c-48b6-93d1-92bdd748ec27","timestamp":"2026-05-05T09:07:22.403Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"ba6294b0-a5fd-44fd-9d04-b07f4e2227ed","version":"2.1.126","gitBranch":"soph/make-list-like-git-log"}
